/* FindArray_r: intermediate level of FindArray, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step), the
   component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace min({ii | ...} \/ {max_IDX + 1}) by the three facts a loop establishes: the
   result is a position or max_IDX + 1, no position before it holds value, and it holds value if
   it is a position. The proof that these facts define the minimum is thus done once, here, away
   from the loop. Same shape as max_array_r of the max-array demonstration. */
REFINEMENT
    FindArray_r

REFINES
    FindArray

SEES
    Ctx_FindArray

OPERATIONS

    pos <-- find(array, value) =
    PRE
        array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        value : INT
    THEN
        pos :( pos : 0..max_IDX + 1 &
               !ii.(ii : 0..pos - 1 => array(ii) /= value) &
               (pos <= max_IDX => array(pos) = value) )
    END

END
